    {
        "content": "<p><code>X</code> and <code>Finset.univ</code> are two different types. What you need is <code>∀ x ∈ Finset.univ, f x ≠ ⊤</code>,  but this can be proved trivially from <code>f_ne_top</code> by introducing an extra variable <code>hx : x ∈ Finset.univ</code>, i.e. something like <code>rw [ENNReal.toReal_sum (fun x hx =&gt; f_ne_top X f M rbound x)]</code> should work (and if you don't like <code>hx</code> as it is not used in this proof, you can replace it with <code>_</code>)</p>",
        "id": 608480671,
        "sender_full_name": "Yongxi Lin (Aaron)",
        "timestamp": 1783352379
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"669043\">Yongxi Lin (Aaron)</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/.5BENNReal.2EtoReal_sum.5D.20proof.20that.20sum.20is.20over.20Fintype.2Euniv.20.3F/near/608480671\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>X</code> and <code>Finset.univ</code> are two different types.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I guess one could even say that <code>Finset.univ</code> is a term, not a type. It's a term of type <code>Finset X</code>.</p>",
        "id": 608544212,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1783372392
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks to both of you.<br>\nIf I understand properly, here</p>\n<ol>\n<li>we introduce a new function that maps each x (provably in Finset.univ) to a proof that <code>f x ≠ ⊤</code>, which produces a lemma that matches our requirements, and </li>\n<li>Lean is smart enough to fill in \"hx\" as required.<br>\nThat's a bit tricky to me <span aria-label=\"grinning\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f600\" role=\"img\" title=\"grinning\">:grinning:</span></li>\n</ol>",
        "id": 608546635,
        "sender_full_name": "Olivier Buffet",
        "timestamp": 1783373541
    }
]